{"version":5,"erd_version":40,"tasks":[{"id":"T1","file":"src/vortex/catalog.py","depends_on":[],"brief":"Edit `src/vortex/catalog.py` only. Add no new imports beyond what the file already has.\n\n1. `CatalogEntry`: add two optional fields, both carried through `model_dump()`/validation: `source_path: str | None = None` (the model files an added entry serves) and `origin: Literal[\"config\", \"local\"] = \"config\"` (import `Literal` from typing if absent).\n\n2. `load_catalog(path, local_path=None)`: loads `path` as today (origin \"config\"). When `local_path` is given AND the file exists, its `{\"entries\": [...]}` rows are loaded with origin forced to \"local\" and merged after the config rows; the merged catalog is validated by the same duplicate public id / duplicate port rules (same messages: \"duplicate public id\", \"duplicate port\"). A missing local file is not an error.\n\n3. `Catalog.add(entry)`: raises `ValueError` whose message contains \"duplicate public id\" or \"duplicate port\" when either collides with an existing entry; otherwise appends to `self.entries` IN PLACE (other components hold this same list).\n\n4. `Catalog.remove(public_id) -> CatalogEntry`: `KeyError` for an unknown id; `ValueError` with a message containing \"config\" for an entry whose origin is \"config\"; otherwise removes it from `self.entries` in place and returns it.\n\n5. `save_local_entries(catalog, local_path)`: writes `{\"entries\": [<every origin \"local\" entry as model_dump(mode=\"json\")>]}` (indent 2) to a temp file beside `local_path`, then `os.replace` onto it. Only local entries are written; config entries never are.\n\nAcceptance: `ruff check` and `mypy --explicit-package-bases src/vortex/catalog.py` clean; the file defines the two new fields and the add/remove/save_local_entries behavior exactly as above.","contracts":["src.vortex.catalog","src.vortex.catalog:Catalog","src.vortex.catalog:CatalogEntry","src.vortex.catalog:load_catalog","src.vortex.catalog:save_local_entries"],"tests":["tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_entries_default_to_config_origin_and_no_source_path","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_load_merges_the_local_file_as_local_origin","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_load_without_a_local_file_is_just_the_config","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_local_entries_colliding_with_config_are_rejected","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_add_appends_and_rejects_duplicates","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_remove_only_removes_local_entries","tests/test_catalog_local.py::test_save_writes_only_local_entries_and_round_trips"]},{"id":"T2","file":"src/vortex/discovery.py","depends_on":["T1"],"brief":"Edit `src/vortex/discovery.py` only.\n\n1. `DiscoveredModel`: add field `path: str | None = None` (field order: after `in_catalog`). It appears in the wire schema of `/api/discovered-models`.\n\n2. Add module constants: `LMS_BIN = Path.home() / \".lmstudio/bin/lms\"` and `LMSTUDIO_MODELS_ROOT = Path.home() / \".lmstudio/models\"`.\n\n3. New `lmstudio_model_paths(run=None, models_root=None) -> dict[str, str]`: `run` is a zero-argument callable returning the stdout text of `lms ls --json`; the default runs `[str(LMS_BIN), \"ls\", \"--json\"]` with `subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10, check=False)` and returns its stdout. The text is a JSON array (see frozen capture `captures/lms-ls.json`); each row with both a `modelKey` and a `path` maps `modelKey -> str(models_root / path)` (`models_root` defaults to `LMSTUDIO_MODELS_ROOT`). ANY exception or non-list JSON returns `{}` — log at debug level, never raise.\n\n4. `discover_models(catalog_entries=None, fetch=None, probes=None, paths=None)`: `paths` is a zero-argument callable returning that map (default `lmstudio_model_paths`). Each DiscoveredModel's `path` is `paths_map.get(key)`. `in_catalog` is true when the key equals an entry's `upstream_alias` (as today) OR the model's path is not None and equals an entry's `source_path` or is one of the strings in an entry's `launch_command`.\n\nAcceptance: ruff and mypy clean; the wire schema of `/api/discovered-models` carries `path`.","contracts":["src.vortex.discovery:lmstudio_model_paths"],"tests":["tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_path_map_joins_cli_paths_onto_the_models_root","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_path_map_is_empty_when_the_listing_cannot_be_read","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_path_map_skips_rows_without_key_or_path","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_discovered_models_carry_their_path_or_none","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_in_catalog_matches_a_path_in_an_entry_launch_command","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_in_catalog_matches_an_entry_source_path","tests/test_discovery_paths.py::test_unrelated_entry_does_not_mark_the_model_in_catalog"]},{"id":"T3","file":"src/vortex/catalog_synth.py","depends_on":["T1","T2"],"brief":"CREATE src/vortex/catalog_synth.py (NEW file, under 150 lines). Constraints: stdlib `os` and `re` only, plus EXACT relative imports: `from .catalog import Catalog, CatalogEntry` and `from .discovery import DiscoveredModel`. No other imports. No global mutable state. Annotate optional values as `X | None`.\n\nDefine:\n- `PORT_RANGE = range(8200, 8300)`\n- `RUNTIME_BINARIES = {\"mlx\": \"/opt/homebrew/bin/mlx-serve\", \"gguf\": \"/opt/homebrew/bin/llama-server\"}`\n- `class SynthesisError(ValueError)`\n- `synthesize_entry(model: DiscoveredModel, catalog: Catalog, binaries=RUNTIME_BINARIES) -> CatalogEntry`\n\nBehavior — checks in this order, each raising SynthesisError with the quoted word in the message:\n1. `model.path` is None → \"no local path known for <key>\" (contains \"path\")\n2. `model.fmt` not a key of `binaries` → \"unsupported format <fmt>\" (contains \"format\")\n3. `model.architecture` is None → \"no architecture reported (not a chat model)\" (contains \"architecture\")\n4. public_id already used, or path equals an entry's `source_path` or is present in its `launch_command` → \"already in the catalog as <id>\" (contains \"already\")\n5. no port of PORT_RANGE free of catalog ports → \"no free port in 8200-8299\" (contains \"port\")\n\npublic_id = `re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9._-]\", \"-\", model.key.lower())`\nport = lowest port in PORT_RANGE not used by any catalog entry\n\nmlx: runtime and engine \"mlx-serve\", launch `[binaries[\"mlx\"], \"--model\", path, \"--serve\", \"--host\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--port\", str(port)]`\ngguf: runtime \"llama-server\", engine \"llama.cpp\", launch `[binaries[\"gguf\"], \"-m\", path, \"--host\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--port\", str(port)]`\n\nready_url `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1/models`, chat_endpoint `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1/chat/completions`, upstream_alias = `os.path.basename(path.rstrip(\"/\"))`, `ram_estimate_gb = round(size_bytes * 1.1 / 1e9, 1)` when size_bytes else None, `exclusive = ram_estimate_gb is not None and ram_estimate_gb > 40`, `source_path = path`, `origin = \"local\"`. Return `CatalogEntry.model_validate(...)` of that dict.\n\nAcceptance: all 9 tests in tests/test_catalog_synth.py pass.","contracts":["src.vortex.catalog_synth","src.vortex.catalog_synth:PORT_RANGE","src.vortex.catalog_synth:RUNTIME_BINARIES","src.vortex.catalog_synth:SynthesisError","src.vortex.catalog_synth:synthesize_entry"],"tests":["tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_a_model_already_in_the_catalog_is_refused","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_gguf_model_becomes_a_llama_server_entry","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_lowest_free_port_skips_ports_the_catalog_uses","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_mlx_model_becomes_an_mlx_serve_entry","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_no_free_port_is_refused","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_port_range_and_binaries_are_the_ceo_policy","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_public_id_is_sanitized_from_the_key","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_ram_estimate_is_size_plus_ten_percent_and_sets_exclusive","tests/test_catalog_synth.py::test_unsynthesizable_models_raise_with_a_reason"]},{"id":"T4","file":"src/vortex/app.py","depends_on":["T3"],"brief":"EDIT src/vortex/app.py. Constraints: NO new dependencies. Extend the existing `from .catalog import ...` line so it also imports `save_local_entries`. Add `from .catalog_synth import SynthesisError, synthesize_entry` next to the other relative imports. No `vortex.models` module exists. No global mutable state.\n\nChanges from current behavior:\n- `build_app` gains keyword `local_catalog_path: Path | None = None`. When `catalog` is None, the app loads `load_catalog(<repo>/config/catalog.json, local_path=<repo>/config/catalog.local.json)` and persists to that local path. When `catalog` is passed explicitly, persistence goes to `local_catalog_path` only if it was given (otherwise adds/removes stay in memory). `model_discovery` is still called with ONLY `catalog_entries=...`.\n- `/api/catalog` rows add `\"origin\"` and `\"source_path\"`.\n- `POST /api/discovered-models/{key}/add`: find `key` in the discovered models (cached list; rescan once if absent) → 404 `{\"detail\": \"...\"}` if absent; `synthesize_entry(model, catalog)` → on SynthesisError 422 `{\"detail\": {\"message\": str(exc), \"key\": key}}`; else `catalog.add`, persist, clear the discovered-model cache, and return 201 `{\"added\": entry.model_dump(mode=\"json\")}`.\n- `POST /api/discovered-models/add-new`: clear the cache, rescan, and for each discovered model with `in_catalog` False try synthesize + add (the catalog grows as it goes, so ports never collide); SynthesisError rows go to `skipped` as `{\"key\", \"reason\"}`. Persist once, clear the cache, return 200 `{\"added\": [<public ids>], \"skipped\": [...]}`.\n- `DELETE /api/catalog/{public_id}`: 404 when unknown; 409 `{\"detail\": {\"message\": ...}}` when origin is \"config\", when the entry is loaded (its port is occupied — `lifecycle.occupying_pid(entry)` is not None) or when an operation for it is active (`ops.active_for(public_id)`); otherwise `catalog.remove`, persist, clear the cache, return 200 `{\"removed\": public_id}`.\n\nAcceptance: all 8 tests in tests/test_catalog_add_api.py pass.","contracts":["route:POST /api/discovered-models/{key}/add","route:POST /api/discovered-models/add-new","route:DELETE /api/catalog/{public_id}","src.vortex.catalog_synth:synthesize_entry","src.vortex.catalog:save_local_entries"],"tests":["tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_add_new_adds_every_synthesizable_new_model_on_distinct_ports","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_add_puts_the_model_in_the_live_catalog_and_the_local_file","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_add_unknown_key_is_404_and_changes_nothing","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_add_unsynthesizable_is_422_with_the_reason","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_added_model_is_no_longer_newly_found","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_remove_deletes_a_local_entry_from_catalog_and_file","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_remove_refuses_a_loaded_local_entry","tests/test_catalog_add_api.py::test_remove_refuses_config_entries_and_unknown_ids"]},{"id":"T5","file":"src/vortex/ui.py","depends_on":[],"brief":"Edit `src/vortex/ui.py` only; `UI_PAGE` is one HTML string. No external asset references.\n\n1. Beside the existing Scan control (`data-act=\"scan-models\"`) add `<button id=\"addnewmodels\">Add all new</button>` and an empty `<div id=\"addresult\"></div>`.\n\n2. Its handler: `document.getElementById(\"addnewmodels\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {` -> `confirm(\"Add every discovered model not yet in Vortex to the loadable list?\")`, `return` on cancel; else `fetch(\"/api/discovered-models/add-new\", { method: \"POST\" })`; on success write \"Added N\" plus each skipped `s.key + \" (\" + s.reason + \")\"` (reading `body.skipped` / `.reason`) into `#addresult`, then call `pollCatalog()` and `pollModels()`; on failure `setError(\"Add failed: \" + message)`.\n\n3. In the discovered-model row renderer: when `!m.in_catalog`, render `<button data-act=\"add-model\" data-key=\"...\">Add</button>`; its click POSTs `\"/api/discovered-models/\" + encodeURIComponent(key) + \"/add\"` with `{ method: \"POST\" }`, then re-polls both lists; failure -> `setError(\"Add failed: \" + <server detail message>)`.\n\n4. In the catalog row renderer: when `m.origin === \"local\"`, render `<button data-act=\"remove-model\" data-id=\"...\">Remove</button>`; its click `confirm(\"Remove <id> from Vortex? The model files are not deleted.\")`, then `fetch(\"/api/catalog/\" + encodeURIComponent(id), { method: \"DELETE\" })`, re-polls both lists; failure -> `setError(\"Remove failed: \" + <detail message>)`.\n\n5. Every `m.*` field the page reads must be returned by `/api/catalog` or `/api/discovered-models`.\n\nAcceptance: ruff and mypy clean; the new controls and handlers exist; no http/https asset URL added.","contracts":[],"tests":["tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_add_all_new_control_sits_with_the_discovered_models_scan","tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_add_all_new_confirms_then_posts","tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_add_all_reports_skips_and_failures","tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_each_new_discovered_model_gets_an_add_control","tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_local_entries_get_a_confirmed_remove_control","tests/test_ui_catalog_add.py::test_successful_changes_refresh_both_lists"]}]}